1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:03,000
[KAZUMA]
Some "Divine Treasure" huh?

2
00:00:03,090 --> 00:00:04,550
♪

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,260
Sure, I knew
there was a time limit,

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,680
but it wore off fast.

5
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:08,760
[gasps]

6
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:10,680
[screams]

7
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:13,310
Eris, if this is your idea
of a joke,

8
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:15,520
I'm not laughin'!

9
00:00:16,730 --> 00:00:18,140
- [AQUA] Hey, Kazuma.
- [KAZUMA] I'm Kazuma.

10
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:20,400
[AQUA] You just love
calling me an "idiot"

11
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,400
but, now I'm sure of something.

12
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,440
You must be, like, an idiot
of the highest caliber,

13
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,900
aren't you?

14
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,440
Oh, come on,
you don't understand!

15
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:29,490
Walkin' around the castle,
everybody was waiting

16
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:30,620
on me hand and foot!

17
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,160
So, I started thinkin'
I could get away

18
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,530
with just about anything!

19
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,200
Then, that makes you
a stupid idiot

20
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:36,830
who really needs to think
about what he did!

21
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:39,210
[KAZUMA]
Man, even Iris was mad at me!

22
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:42,630
Don't know if Big Brother
can go on living!

23
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,960
[NOBLE 06-A (F)] Oh, look
there, it's the big talker.

24
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:47,090
[NOBLE 06-C (M)] Why
Lady Dustiness ever associated

25
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:49,380
with someone like that
is quite beyond me.

26
00:00:49,470 --> 00:00:50,970
[NOBLE 06-A (F)]
It makes no sense!

27
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,930
[CLAIRE] Princess Iris has
already retired for the night.

28
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,430
[KAZUMA]
She has?

29
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,390
So, this is goodbye.

30
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:59,980
You're free to stay here
and enjoy the festivities.

31
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:02,310
[CLAIRE] Assuming that
you actually have the nerve

32
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,940
to do so.

33
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:05,690
[squeaks]

34
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:07,190
[CLAIRE]
Konosuba.

35
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:09,440
[KAZUMA]
This sucks!

36
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:10,950
What the hell
is that chick's problem?

37
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:13,780
Even at the very end, she just
had to get some digs in!

38
00:01:13,870 --> 00:01:16,290
I mean, sure, it's my fault,
I totally admit that!

39
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:17,410
But, I just wanted to stay

40
00:01:17,490 --> 00:01:19,870
in the castle
a little bit longer!

41
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:21,250
[thudding]

42
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,580
Huh?

43
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:24,920
[door creaking opens]

44
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:30,970
You can keep asking,
but my answer won't change.

45
00:01:31,050 --> 00:01:33,850
Now, now there's no need
to act like that.

46
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:35,810
Right, guess I might
as well tell you,

47
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:37,640
the Divine Treasure
that swaps bodies

48
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,140
is here in the castle.

49
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:41,100
But I don't see
what's so dangerous about it.

50
00:01:42,810 --> 00:01:45,020
Well, the thing is,
if for any reason,

51
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:47,440
the body that's been
swapped gets killed

52
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,740
it then becomes
a permanent change.

53
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:50,990
Huh?

54
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,410
When used a certain way,
this thing can potentially

55
00:01:53,490 --> 00:01:55,740
let a person
to go on living forever.

56
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:58,040
Once your body slows down
and starts aging,

57
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:00,660
you simply find a young,
healthy person to switch with

58
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:02,920
and then kill them
once you're in their body.

59
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,790
That sounds
pretty messed up to me!

60
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,170
Maybe we should
tell someone and--

61
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:08,170
That's the worst thing
either of us could do.

62
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:10,460
If people hear
what this item's capable of

63
00:02:10,550 --> 00:02:12,380
you do know
what'll happen next, right?

64
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,380
♪

65
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:15,930
'Cause I have no doubt.

66
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,970
Nobles will come from all over

67
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,520
hoping to steal it
for themselves.

68
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,270
[KAZUMA] It's the power
of eternal life, huh?

69
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:27,150
I've chosen to share
all this with you

70
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,860
'cause I know
you won't misuse it,

71
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,400
in case you're wondering.

72
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,490
[KAZUMA]
Huh?

73
00:02:31,570 --> 00:02:33,610
Does she seriously
trust me this much?

74
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,280
[CHRIS] So, it seems
you and the princess

75
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:38,580
have become playmates lately,
haven't you?

76
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:41,790
Well, if you think
you're feeling up to it

77
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,040
wanna go play now?

78
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,460
[giggles]

79
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:45,620
Huh?

80
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,630
[indistinct chatter]

81
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:51,170
We're in luck.

82
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:52,970
Since there's
a big party going on

83
00:02:53,050 --> 00:02:54,800
the security seems light.

84
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,260
Yeah, it does.

85
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,850
Hey, why're you
dressed like that?

86
00:02:58,930 --> 00:03:02,100
I don't want anyone
knowing who I am, either.

87
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,640
A really shady guy working
in a magic item shop

88
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:06,400
handed me this mask.

89
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,860
He said it's one of the hottest
things in the store.

90
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:10,110
Oh?

91
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,150
Right, time to go.

92
00:03:12,230 --> 00:03:14,150
[CHRIS]
You ready, minion?

93
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,110
Yep, I'm ready
when you are, big lady.

94
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,200
Let's move.

95
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,080
[sighs]

96
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:21,740
Look, could you not
refer to me as "Big Lady?"

97
00:03:21,830 --> 00:03:23,370
Then maybe you
shouldn't call me "minion."

98
00:03:23,450 --> 00:03:25,160
You ever think about that?

99
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:28,000
I'm the one who made a name
for herself as a noble thief.

100
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,460
You do remember, right?

101
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:31,800
Okay, let's go.

102
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,260
We should settle this
over rock-paper-scissors.

103
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,340
Sounds good, you're on!

104
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:38,180
[KAZUMA]
Bring it!

105
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,680
- [KAZUMA] Rock, paper...
- [CHRIS] Rock, paper...

106
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,100
[crickets chirping]

107
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:42,180
[CHRIS]
Tell me, assistant,

108
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:44,390
is that where
we'll find the princess?

109
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:46,600
Yeah, right, boss.

110
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:49,690
[KAZUMA] Of all the times
to lose at rock-paper-scissors.

111
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:52,730
Even I can't manage scaling
a castle wall that high.

112
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:54,940
Snipe!

113
00:03:55,030 --> 00:03:56,150
♪

114
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,950
[metal clanging]

115
00:03:58,030 --> 00:03:59,780
♪

116
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:04,450
Aah, you're pretty handy, assistant.

117
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:05,830
♪

118
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:07,920
[footsteps]

119
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
♪

120
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,590
It's been
smooth sailing so far.

121
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:16,920
[gasps]

122
00:04:17,010 --> 00:04:18,970
♪

123
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:22,220
Hey, boss, my enemy detection's
picking something...

124
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:26,020
[sniffing]

125
00:04:27,810 --> 00:04:29,310
Hey, assistant?

126
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:31,520
Since you have the Lurk skill,
do we really need

127
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:33,520
to stick so close
together like this?

128
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:35,690
This is no time
to be careless, boss!

129
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:37,440
We can't afford
to take up much space!

130
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:39,700
- Get closer!
- Whoa, that's too close!

131
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:42,280
This is to maintain the world's
peace, and, uh, other stuff!

132
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,950
Hang in there, please,
oh, you have to!

133
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,700
If you don't stop
what you're doing right now

134
00:04:45,790 --> 00:04:47,790
you're gonna bring
about Eris' divine wrath!

135
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:50,170
Intruders,
they're here in the castle!

136
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:52,170
[GUARD 06-B (M)]
Get out here, men, now!

137
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,420
[horn blowing]

138
00:04:57,590 --> 00:04:59,930
See what can happen
when you yell like that, boss?

139
00:05:00,010 --> 00:05:01,220
We're gonna need
to have a long talk

140
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:02,300
when all this is over!

141
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,640
Whatever, now's not
the time to be fighting!

142
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:06,470
[CHRIS]
I have heard enough out of you!

143
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:09,270
[GUARD 06-C (M)] Princess Iris
is on the top floor, stop them!

144
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:11,770
[panting]

145
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:14,150
Create Water!

146
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:15,770
[KAZUMA]
Freeze.

147
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:17,780
Whoa...

148
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,570
[grunting]

149
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:21,990
[GUARD 06-C (M)]
Oh, my coccyx.

150
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:24,320
- [GUARD 06-A (M)] Stop!
- Nice move, my assistant.

151
00:05:24,410 --> 00:05:27,160
Hey, try complimenting less
and helping out more, boss!

152
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:28,160
Okay.

153
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:30,580
Stand back as I show you
what I can do?

154
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:32,500
♪

155
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:34,500
Wire Trap!

156
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:39,420
Whoa, you could've
used that a little sooner.

157
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:41,800
All right, that should
buy us some time.

158
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,970
[CLAIRE] You just cut off
your only escape route.

159
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,760
[sword scraping]

160
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:49,810
And now you two
don't have anywhere to run!

161
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,640
It's gone from bad to worse.

162
00:05:52,730 --> 00:05:54,230
[gasps]
Up there.

163
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:55,900
[CHRIS]
That's how we're getting out.

164
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,730
[KAZUMA]
What? No.

165
00:05:57,820 --> 00:06:01,240
Wait, if I'm gonna be kicked
out of the capital tomorrow

166
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,740
then I would rather take care
of all this tonight!

167
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:04,820
Huh?

168
00:06:04,910 --> 00:06:07,740
Hang on, since when have you
ever said something like that?

169
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:09,290
[gasps]

170
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,700
[KAZUMA]
She's right.

171
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:13,460
What the hell's gotten into me?

172
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:14,710
Gotta calm down

173
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:16,920
I'm normally
way more levelheaded.

174
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,710
Yeah, once I get back to Axel,
I can finally relax a little.

175
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,930
[IRIS] With the way
things are these days

176
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:25,930
it's not a good time
to immerse myself in studies.

177
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:29,020
So, uh, I was hoping you would
play this game with me.

178
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,100
Please?

179
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:33,020
Simple, you aren't
like the others.

180
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:36,230
Everyone dotes on me,
but you never do that.

181
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:38,650
You're rude and so honest.

182
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:41,070
Hey, I wasn't asking you
to roll out

183
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,820
a huge list of complaints.

184
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:46,410
Right, and that's exactly what
I've been trying to tell you.

185
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:47,950
[chuckles]

186
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:51,370
[sighs]

187
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:52,450
[gasps]

188
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:54,750
Listen, boss I, uh...

189
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:58,290
I think I'm gonna
have to get serious.

190
00:06:58,380 --> 00:06:59,420
[CHRIS]
You what?

191
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,840
- Enough chatter!
- [sword slashing]

192
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,590
[gasps]

193
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,130
Uh-oh!

194
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:07,050
[screams]

195
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:11,310
So, um... what skill's that?

196
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,600
[sword clanging]

197
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:16,900
[chuckles]

198
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:22,070
Sorry this one's
my little secret.

199
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,320
Top condition! Top condition!

200
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:27,030
I'm not sure why,
but I am in top condition!

201
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:28,160
[gasps]

202
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,370
[laughing]

203
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:30,740
[KAZUMA]
Increased magic power!

204
00:07:30,830 --> 00:07:32,200
Improved circulation!

205
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:33,500
A clearer complexion!

206
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,750
Tonight, I'll display
my true strength!

207
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,120
[gasps]

208
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:38,920
[laughs]
Look out!

209
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,340
We are the Silver-Haired
Thief Brigade!

210
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:42,710
[grunts]

211
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,550
Spare yourselves
excruciating pain

212
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,630
and clear a path.

213
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,010
[screams]

214
00:07:50,430 --> 00:07:51,850
♪

215
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:54,430
[GUARD 06-C (M)]
He's strong, amazing!

216
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:57,690
[GUARD 06-D (M)]
Even with that weird mask!

217
00:07:57,770 --> 00:07:59,060
[screams]

218
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:00,150
[gasps]

219
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:02,690
Lightning, Skill Bind!

220
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,360
[RAIN]
What?

221
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,820
Hey, I don't like
"Silver-Haired Thief Brigade!"

222
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:09,280
Starting now,
you can be the boss.

223
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:11,660
So, I think we should go
with "Masked Thief Brigade!"

224
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:13,240
[KAZUMA]
That's not for me.

225
00:08:13,330 --> 00:08:16,370
I'd rather not be treated
like a criminal mastermind.

226
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:18,710
So, guess what,
I don't want to, either!

227
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:20,790
[laser firing]

228
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,840
♪

229
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,550
[footsteps]

230
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:29,590
[MITSURUGI] Claire,
you're facing a vicious foe.

231
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,800
[BOTH]
Hmm.

232
00:08:30,890 --> 00:08:33,180
♪

233
00:08:34,930 --> 00:08:36,640
But, now, I am here.

234
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:41,150
Please allow a Swordmaster
to bring down this masked man!

235
00:08:43,610 --> 00:08:45,980
♪

236
00:08:46,070 --> 00:08:47,530
And, to you,

237
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:50,990
I leave the silver-haired boy
to be swiftly dispatched.

238
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:53,330
♪

239
00:08:53,410 --> 00:08:54,740
[CHRIS]
Hey, assistant.

240
00:08:55,950 --> 00:08:58,410
Do you think I look like
a boy that much?

241
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,620
Maybe he noticed you're built
straight up and down.

242
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:02,290
[whimpering]

243
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:04,210
It's time to get a grip!

244
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,090
This is a critical juncture!

245
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:08,260
As soon as I Steal
his cursed sword.

246
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:10,720
It would appear that
you're going to use Steal.

247
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,220
But, unfortunately...

248
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,310
ever since losing
to one who wields it,

249
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,640
I've prepared counter-measures,
where I--

250
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,180
Steal!

251
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:19,730
It's no use!

252
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,730
- Wait... [gasps]
- Freeze...

253
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:25,860
[KAZUMA]
And one more, Freeze.

254
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,900
[whimpering]

255
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,070
[groaning]

256
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,320
♪

257
00:09:32,490 --> 00:09:33,370
Huh?!

258
00:09:33,570 --> 00:09:34,950
Hmm...

259
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:37,580
Huh, Create Water!

260
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,580
[screams]

261
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,710
- Sir Mitsurugi?
- Sir Mitsurugi?

262
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:42,790
[laughing]

263
00:09:42,870 --> 00:09:44,080
[KAZUMA]
What idiot would dare take

264
00:09:44,170 --> 00:09:45,670
a Swordmaster head-on?

265
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:47,710
Your weakness
is overconfidence!

266
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,760
[laughing]

267
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:52,430
Oh, so these
are negative emotions.

268
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:55,050
Savory, quite savory indeed.

269
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,470
[CLAIRE]
Damn you!

270
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:58,060
[KAZUMA]
Away!

271
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,430
[laughing]

272
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:02,100
I would advise looking after
that man immediately!

273
00:10:02,190 --> 00:10:03,690
Sir Mitsurugi!

274
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:06,150
[CLAIRE] Quickly, Rain,
he'll need healing magic!

275
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:07,230
[RAIN]
C-Coming!

276
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,650
Boss, this way!

277
00:10:08,730 --> 00:10:09,730
Oh, no!

278
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,650
You can't escape
with Princess Iris ahead!

279
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,530
Stop them, all of you!

280
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:16,950
[all gasping]

281
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:19,040
[laughing]

282
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,370
It seems that
we're nearly to Iris' room!

283
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:22,790
Copy that, assistant!

284
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:25,250
[KAZUMA]
Top condition, top condition!

285
00:10:25,330 --> 00:10:27,750
I'm in top condition now!

286
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,460
[sword clanking]

287
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:31,670
That is far enough, intruder.

288
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,930
To protect the kingdom,
and its royalty

289
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:36,300
I shall not allow you to pass.

290
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:37,560
[DARKNESS]
Therefore...

291
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,060
So-So, what are we
gonna do now, assistant?

292
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,730
[DARKNESS] Hey, do not close
the door on me!

293
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:45,560
What in the world
are you two trying to...

294
00:10:45,650 --> 00:10:46,810
[gasps]

295
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:48,900
[both whimpering]

296
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:50,280
♪

297
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:52,110
[IRIS]
Intruders.

298
00:10:52,190 --> 00:10:55,030
I am quite impressed
that you made it this far.

299
00:10:55,110 --> 00:10:57,240
But, the Hero's blood's
in my veins

300
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,370
and, like the rest
of my family,

301
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:00,370
I've worked hard
to maintain that strength.

302
00:11:01,290 --> 00:11:02,580
I swear upon this ring

303
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:03,960
that has been passed down
throughout my--

304
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,330
Move out of the way!

305
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:08,000
A couple of intruders
will be no match for my--

306
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:12,210
[gasps]
They look so cool!

307
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:13,840
What should we do now,
Darkness?

308
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,970
These noble thieves
have incredible style!

309
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:18,140
[MEGUMIN] This one's wearing
such a unique mask

310
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:20,140
and that black
costume's amazing!

311
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:21,220
What's your name?

312
00:11:21,310 --> 00:11:24,060
Please tell me you've already
selected a name for your gang!

313
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:26,480
And Bind.

314
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,560
[gasps]

315
00:11:27,650 --> 00:11:28,770
That's so cool!

316
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:30,520
Oh, my, I know!

317
00:11:30,610 --> 00:11:33,030
[AQUA]
Sacred Break Spell!

318
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:36,070
[both whimpering]

319
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,910
[chuckles]

320
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,990
Really sorry to break it to ya

321
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:45,370
but all of your luck ran out
when you ran into me.

322
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:47,670
I have no idea
what you're looking for

323
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:49,960
but if I catch the two of you

324
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:54,050
bet that'll be enough to earn
me some more fancy bubbly!

325
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:56,930
Now, be good thieves
and surrender, okay?

326
00:11:57,010 --> 00:11:59,390
[KAZUMA]
That little...

327
00:11:59,470 --> 00:12:00,970
What's the hold up, Darkness?

328
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:03,310
Megumin's totally lost it
for some weird reason,

329
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:05,140
which means
you're our only hope!

330
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:06,560
Right!

331
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,610
Okay, use Steal
when we're making our escape.

332
00:12:09,690 --> 00:12:11,400
On the Divine Treasure, right?

333
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,400
But, won't your Steal be, uh...

334
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,190
You think it only works
on underwear, huh?

335
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:18,780
- Princess Iris!
- You coward!

336
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,620
Such dirty tricks!

337
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:22,830
Let's attack them
from both sides!

338
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:23,910
[gasps]

339
00:12:23,990 --> 00:12:27,210
And now
you will face my full...

340
00:12:27,290 --> 00:12:31,590
- Come on!
- Face my full... powered swing!

341
00:12:31,670 --> 00:12:33,590
♪

342
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,840
Yep, that's our
knucklehead Crusader!

343
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:38,010
[gasps]

344
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:39,930
Princess Iris!

345
00:12:40,010 --> 00:12:41,260
Now!

346
00:12:41,350 --> 00:12:44,100
- Steal!
- Steal!

347
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,230
[glass shattering]

348
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:50,480
Yes, all right, let's go!

349
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:52,190
[CHRIS]
We'll have to jump from here!

350
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:53,860
Where's my necklace?

351
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:56,110
Now I dunno
what you just ripped off

352
00:12:56,190 --> 00:12:59,150
but I am not gonna stand here
and let you get away with it!

353
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,860
What an idiot,
stop making problems!

354
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:03,280
[grunts]

355
00:13:03,370 --> 00:13:05,540
[KAZUMA]
Damn it all!

356
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,500
♪

357
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,290
They're gone!

358
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:14,500
Wow, that's so cool!

359
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:15,840
[sighs]

360
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,010
♪

361
00:13:20,930 --> 00:13:22,180
You've got to calm yourself!

362
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:24,430
Just calm down, please!

363
00:13:24,510 --> 00:13:25,930
[yelping]
Let go of my head!

364
00:13:26,010 --> 00:13:27,600
You're gonna do
some serious damage!

365
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:30,310
I didn't want to,
but she forced me into it!

366
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:32,520
This was all Chris' idea!

367
00:13:32,650 --> 00:13:34,400
Excuse me,
what is your problem?

368
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,610
Ow, ow, ow!

369
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:37,280
You recovered
the Divine Treasure

370
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:40,070
because it was
too dangerous, is that right?

371
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,780
Then, why not tell me
that from the very beginning?

372
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:45,490
My-My assistant didn't want
a link between you

373
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:46,490
and the noble thief.

374
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,790
He thought it could only
put you in a bad position!

375
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:50,540
[crying]

376
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:53,250
Co-Come on,
don't tell her everything!

377
00:13:53,330 --> 00:13:55,210
[whimpering]

378
00:13:55,290 --> 00:13:57,250
Honestly, you two.

379
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:59,670
Is anything else
being hidden from me?

380
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,630
[grunting]

381
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:04,340
Oh, it seems there is.

382
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:08,680
Wait, is that her...

383
00:14:08,770 --> 00:14:12,230
I figured it would work better
if we did it at the same time.

384
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:13,980
Why does your Steal
only work on things

385
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:15,350
that aren't meant to be stolen?

386
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,360
Well at least it wasn't
panties this time!

387
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,070
Okay, that's not the point!

388
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:21,650
♪

389
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,410
Listen, Kazuma.

390
00:14:24,490 --> 00:14:27,120
Do not lose this
and tell no one you have it.

391
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,370
Do you understand?

392
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:30,080
Keeping this secret is vital,

393
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,500
so take it
to the grave with you.

394
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:32,870
Whoa, knock it off, would ya!

395
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,210
If it's really that important,

396
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:35,670
I can say I found
the ring somewhere

397
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:36,750
and give it right back!

398
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:38,380
- Idiot!
- [screams]

399
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:41,760
This ring was intended
for the princess' engagement,

400
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,050
to be removed
and worn by her true love.

401
00:14:44,130 --> 00:14:45,430
[gasps]

402
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:47,970
Now, with it being stolen,
the idea of some

403
00:14:48,050 --> 00:14:50,390
random adventurer finding it.

404
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:52,600
If you returned the ring
out of good will

405
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:55,310
you would still be killed
to keep it all under wraps.

406
00:14:55,390 --> 00:14:56,980
Yeah, that's pretty scary!

407
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,480
Princess Iris,
she loved that ring

408
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:01,400
and always held onto it.

409
00:15:01,490 --> 00:15:04,530
So, you must never forget,
take good care of it

410
00:15:04,610 --> 00:15:06,240
and never tell
anyone about this.

411
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:08,240
♪

412
00:15:09,830 --> 00:15:11,240
[sighs]

413
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:18,210
[RAIN] We weren't aware
of the necklace's

414
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:19,420
dangerous power.

415
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:23,470
Thank you for informing us,
Lady Dustiness.

416
00:15:23,550 --> 00:15:25,380
Yes.

417
00:15:25,470 --> 00:15:28,640
But, you, on the other hand,
you were absolutely useless,

418
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,680
yet again,
on the night in question.

419
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,390
[whimpering]

420
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:33,980
[IRIS]
Could it be...

421
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:37,150
that the thieves did this
in an effort to protect me?

422
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:39,900
Well, if that's so,
then it would mean

423
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:42,190
the rumors we've been hearing
have all been truthful,

424
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,650
they really are noble.

425
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:45,110
I doubt it.

426
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:48,160
However, if there
is some validity to this

427
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,700
then I have to admit,
they are quite impressive.

428
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:53,540
[KAZUMA]
What was that?

429
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:55,540
Do you mean
the man wearing the mask?

430
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:57,370
Oh, he was so incredible!

431
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:59,420
That mask,
and that black costume.

432
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:01,550
They all speak
directly to my values!

433
00:16:01,630 --> 00:16:04,960
Next time he's here, I have
to ask him for an autograph!

434
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:07,220
[KAZUMA]
Oh, man, this is a tough one.

435
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:09,430
I really wanna tell 'em
it was me.

436
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,680
[gasps]

437
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,470
[AQUA] What's the matter
with you, Kazuma?

438
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:14,890
How come you're grinning
like that, it's creepy.

439
00:16:14,970 --> 00:16:16,140
Yes, she's right.

440
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:18,520
What are you suddenly
so happy about?

441
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,690
[whimpering]

442
00:16:20,770 --> 00:16:21,860
[IRIS]
I agree.

443
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,030
In regard to that noble thief.

444
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:26,780
I must say, I was impressed.

445
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:29,450
[KAZUMA] Wait a minute,
is this the thing

446
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:32,070
where she actually
realizes who it really was?

447
00:16:33,870 --> 00:16:36,120
I'm sure that, in the end,
the two of them

448
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,160
did what they did,

449
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,880
because they felt
genuinely concerned for me.

450
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:43,710
But, as I said, when it comes
to that particular noble thief.

451
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:45,630
[deep sigh]

452
00:16:45,710 --> 00:16:48,420
I think I may be
a fan of his, myself.

453
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:51,760
[KAZUMA]
Okay, time for the big reveal.

454
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:53,260
What is the matter, Kazuma?

455
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:54,890
Why did you stand up
so suddenly?

456
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:57,390
Come on, you can tell me,
no need to make me guess!

457
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,810
Do you need to go pee,
is that it?

458
00:16:58,890 --> 00:17:00,310
[DARKNESS]
Pitiful, if you will excuse me,

459
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:01,940
I can remove this fool!

460
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:03,730
Okay, I'll pee right here then!

461
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:05,320
Let go
or I'll Drain Touch your--

462
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,480
[IRIS]
I wonder.

463
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:08,780
Where are they?

464
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:10,780
And what are they doing
right now?

465
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:12,240
Mainly...

466
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:15,330
that attractive
silver-haired thief.

467
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:17,700
♪

468
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,120
[sighs]

469
00:17:21,830 --> 00:17:24,340
[KAZUMA]
Yeah, Konosuban.

470
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:26,460
[IRIS]
I'm sad to see you go, but...

471
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:29,420
[sighing]

472
00:17:30,630 --> 00:17:34,930
...Elder Brother, if possible
I do have one request.

473
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:36,180
[gasps]

474
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:39,560
Please allow me to speak,
Princess Iris.

475
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:41,060
[gasps]

476
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:46,780
This man has taken down many
of the Devil King's generals.

477
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:50,490
In fact, he may even defeat
the Devil King, in due time.

478
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:54,070
But that is a difficult mission
as I'm sure you can imagine.

479
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:58,120
So, as he faces down
such a dismaying task

480
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:01,160
could you offer him
some words of encouragement?

481
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:04,580
[KAZUMA] Hang on just a minute
what the hell did she just say?

482
00:18:04,670 --> 00:18:07,000
He wants to beat
the Devil King?

483
00:18:07,090 --> 00:18:08,170
Is that true?

484
00:18:08,250 --> 00:18:10,630
Please tell me, Elder Brother,
is that really something

485
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,050
you have in your plans?

486
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:14,090
[KAZUMA]
Yeah, right, I could never...

487
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:16,970
[whimpering]

488
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,510
♪

489
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,180
[clearing throat]

490
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:22,480
Well, y'know,
if I get the chance,

491
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:25,060
I'd definitely consider
slaying him,

492
00:18:25,150 --> 00:18:27,770
I...guess.

493
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:29,740
[all chuckle]

494
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:32,030
I just know you can do it,
Elder Brother!

495
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:34,200
I wish you good luck
in defeating him!

496
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:37,620
That's it,
I can't take this anymore!

497
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,700
Could you please stop
calling him "Elder Brother?"

498
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:42,620
After all, you do have
an actual older brother, right?

499
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:45,080
You want to fawn over someone,
try that with him!

500
00:18:45,170 --> 00:18:47,920
Besides, I'm gonna be the one
who takes down the Devil King,

501
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,960
so Kazuma won't have
anything to do!

502
00:18:50,050 --> 00:18:51,920
No, maybe you're the one
who doesn't understand!

503
00:18:52,010 --> 00:18:53,340
Elder Brother
is my Elder Brother!

504
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:55,760
So, why is it wrong for me
to refer to him that way?

505
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:57,350
Besides, if you were the one
who brought down

506
00:18:57,430 --> 00:18:59,470
the Devil King, then there'd
be no point to it at all!

507
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,100
This is something
I want him to do!

508
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,390
Not you,
am I making myself clear?

509
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,100
I ask you to stop
and you start spamming

510
00:19:04,190 --> 00:19:05,190
the Elder Brother button?

511
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:07,230
You wanna pick a fight,
'cause, get ready to lose!

512
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:08,690
Well, we'll just
see about that!

513
00:19:08,770 --> 00:19:11,230
We royals are all
pretty strong, you know!

514
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,900
You dare challenge me,
"princess!"

515
00:19:12,990 --> 00:19:13,990
Stop this at once!

516
00:19:14,070 --> 00:19:16,870
The two of you were getting
along so well yesterday!

517
00:19:16,950 --> 00:19:19,490
[CLAIRE] Princess Iris, you
must try and restrain yourself!

518
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:21,410
You've never been
in a fight before!

519
00:19:21,490 --> 00:19:23,870
- Please, Princess.
- [sighs]

520
00:19:24,210 --> 00:19:27,670
So, what was it
you were gonna ask me?

521
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:29,210
[KAZUMA]
Anything you like.

522
00:19:29,290 --> 00:19:31,380
[sighs]

523
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,090
Why yes, of course.

524
00:19:33,170 --> 00:19:34,590
I wanted to ask you...

525
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:37,010
[gasps]

526
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:38,800
♪

527
00:19:38,890 --> 00:19:40,430
Hmm.

528
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:43,350
♪

529
00:19:43,430 --> 00:19:46,230
Since we didn't have
a chance to settle our game.

530
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:49,610
I wondered if you'd come
and play with me again.

531
00:19:49,690 --> 00:19:51,230
[chuckles]

532
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:53,230
♪

533
00:19:59,370 --> 00:20:00,490
- [KAZUMA] KO!
- [AQUA] NO!

534
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:01,870
- [DARKNESS] SU!
- [MEGUMIN] BA!

535
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:05,290
[screams]

536
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:07,210
You really need
to quiet down.

537
00:20:07,290 --> 00:20:10,420
Go outside of town if you want
to cause such a disturbance.

538
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,840
Things were going well,
and then you screwed me over!

539
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,630
[KAZUMA] When you started in
with all that crap

540
00:20:14,710 --> 00:20:16,340
about me bringing down
the Devil King,

541
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:18,800
Iris probably had to totally
change her plans!

542
00:20:18,890 --> 00:20:20,140
Bet she wanted me
to stay there,

543
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:24,060
or she wanted to go out with me
or maybe even sleep in my bed!

544
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:26,270
Now, that
is utterly ridiculous.

545
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:28,270
After one week,
you think you are capable

546
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:29,810
of convincing somebody like her

547
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:32,270
to fall head over heels
in love with you?

548
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:34,320
[DARKNESS]
Time to face reality.

549
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,610
Promise you won't drag me
back out there!

550
00:20:36,690 --> 00:20:39,820
I don't wanna be fact-checked
about any of this stuff!

551
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:41,870
[whimpering]

552
00:20:41,950 --> 00:20:45,790
[KAZUMA] For the time being
let me dream a little more.

553
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:49,880
Your most precious ring
stolen by thieves.

554
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:52,250
We deserve
to receive your punishment.

555
00:20:53,170 --> 00:20:55,960
[IRIS] I know the two of you
did everything you could.

556
00:20:56,050 --> 00:20:57,720
So, please, don't be upset.

557
00:20:58,930 --> 00:21:00,380
We're grateful for your mercy.

558
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,470
Hmm.

559
00:21:03,550 --> 00:21:05,720
♪

560
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:09,810
[IRIS] A special rule
has been linked to that ring.

561
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:11,940
Whoever shows true courage
and manages

562
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:13,980
to slay the Devil King

563
00:21:14,070 --> 00:21:15,690
will be commended,
and given the right

564
00:21:15,770 --> 00:21:17,860
to take the Princess
as their bride.

565
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,570
Big Brother.

566
00:21:22,070 --> 00:21:24,870
I hope you keep
my ring close to you

567
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,370
and take good care of it.

568
00:22:57,670 --> 00:22:59,500
♪

569
00:22:59,590 --> 00:23:01,170
[ALDARP]
My Divine Treasure.

570
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:03,300
Not only was it stolen
by the thief,

571
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:04,970
but they've taken things
a step further

572
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:07,100
by sealing it away as well?

573
00:23:07,180 --> 00:23:09,260
Find it, now!

574
00:23:09,350 --> 00:23:11,020
[DEVIL 06-A (M)]
That isn't possible.

575
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:14,140
If the Divine Treasure's
been sealed

576
00:23:14,230 --> 00:23:16,520
then there's nothing I can do.

577
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:19,570
You are little more
than a useless wretch!

578
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:21,230
[ALDARP]
Must I wait forever?

579
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,860
When are you actually
going to grant my wish?

580
00:23:23,950 --> 00:23:27,370
[breathing heavily]

581
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:32,750
[SYLVIA]
It's your devoted Sylvia!

582
00:23:32,830 --> 00:23:35,750
And I am really starting
to get into this vacation.

583
00:23:35,830 --> 00:23:37,580
I find it so liberating!

584
00:23:37,670 --> 00:23:38,880
And extremely satisfying!

585
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,050
It seems...

